sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant RsaKeyManagerScreen
    participant BiometricHelper
    participant AuthRepository
    participant Isolate as compute() isolate<br/>(_generateKeyPairIsolate)
    participant EncryptionService
    participant SecureStorage as FlutterSecureStorage
    participant Firestore as Firestore (users,<br/>rsa_key_manager, preferences)

    rect rgb(247,247,247)
    Note over RsaKeyManagerScreen,Firestore: Vault entry gate
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: initState() -> addPostFrameCallback(_authenticate)
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>BiometricHelper: authenticate("Unlock RSA Key Vault")
    alt authentication fails
        BiometricHelper-->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: false
        RsaKeyManagerScreen->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: Navigator.pop(context)
    else authentication succeeds
        BiometricHelper-->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: true
        RsaKeyManagerScreen->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: _gateChecked = true
        RsaKeyManagerScreen->>AuthRepository: updateLastVaultAccess(uid)
        AuthRepository->>Firestore: users/{uid}/profile/preferences.set(<br/>{lastVaultAccessAt: serverTimestamp()}, merge:true)
    end
    end

    rect rgb(247,247,247)
    Note over User,Firestore: Generate / Regenerate (no second biometric prompt)
    User->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: tap "Generate Keys" / "Regenerate Keys"
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>User: _showConfirmDialog() bottom sheet
    User-->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: confirm
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>Isolate: compute(_generateKeyPairIsolate, null)
    Isolate->>EncryptionService: generateRsaKeyPairSync()
    Note right of Isolate: FortunaRandom seeded Random.secure()<br/>RSAKeyGenerator(65537, 2048, 64)
    Isolate-->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: AsymmetricKeyPair{ publicKey, privateKey }
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>EncryptionService: encodePublicKey() / encodePrivateKey()
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>AuthRepository: computeFingerprint(pubKeyJson) -> SHA-256 hex

    opt regenerate (existing key)
        RsaKeyManagerScreen->>SecureStorage: write(privateKeyStorageKey, privKeyJson)
        Note right of SecureStorage: new key written FIRST -<br/>old key superseded immediately
    end

    rect rgb(255,255,255)
    Note over RsaKeyManagerScreen,Firestore: Atomic WriteBatch (3 docs)
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>Firestore: users/{uid}.update({publicKey: pubKeyJson})
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>Firestore: users/{uid}/rsa_key_manager/{auto}.set(<br/>{action:'regenerated', timestamp,<br/>publicKeyHash, deviceInfo})
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>Firestore: users/{uid}/profile/preferences.set(<br/>{keyVaultCreatedAt: serverTimestamp()}, merge:true)
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>Firestore: batch.commit()
    end

    RsaKeyManagerScreen-->>User: SnackBar "RSA keys regenerated successfully."<br/>pop back to ReceiverScreen
    end

    rect rgb(247,247,247)
    Note over User,SecureStorage: Delete (separate destructive action, biometric-gated by vault entry)
    User->>RsaKeyManagerScreen: tap "Delete Keys" -> _showConfirmDialog()
    RsaKeyManagerScreen->>AuthRepository: deleteKeyPair(uid)
    Note over AuthRepository,Firestore: WriteBatch (2 docs)
    AuthRepository->>Firestore: users/{uid}.update({publicKey: FieldValue.delete()})
    AuthRepository->>Firestore: users/{uid}/rsa_key_manager/{auto}.set(<br/>{action:'deleted', publicKeyHash:null, deviceInfo})
    AuthRepository->>Firestore: batch.commit()
    AuthRepository->>SecureStorage: delete(privateKeyStorageKey)
    Note right of SecureStorage: deleted only AFTER Firestore success -<br/>keeps both stores consistent on failure
    end
